Description: CVE-2026-33999 - Fix buffer re-use in _XkbSetCompatMap
 If the "compat" buffer has previously been truncated, there will be
 unused space in the buffer. The code uses this space, but does not
 update the number of valid entries in the buffer.
 .
 In the best case, this leads to the new compat entries being ignored.
 In the worst case, if there are any "skipped" compat entries, the
 number of valid entries will be corrupted, potentially leading to a
 buffer read overrun when processing a future request.
 .
 Set the number of used "compat" entries when re-using previously
 allocated space in the buffer.
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/commit/b024ae1749ee58c6fbf863b9a1f5dc440fee2e1b
Author: Peter Harris <pharris2@rocketsoftware.com>
Last-Update: 2026-01-15

--- a/xkb/xkb.c
+++ b/xkb/xkb.c
@@ -3003,7 +3003,7 @@ _XkbSetCompatMap(ClientPtr client, DeviceIntPtr dev,
                 return BadAlloc;
             }
         }
-        else if (req->truncateSI) {
+        else if (req->truncateSI || req->firstSI + req->nSI > compat->num_si) {
             compat->num_si = req->firstSI + req->nSI;
         }
         sym = &compat->sym_interpret[req->firstSI];
Description: CVE-2026-56000 not applicable — vulnerable ordering absent in xorg-server 1.20.11
 Documentation-only placeholder for Debian bullseye (2:1.20.11-1+deb11u17).
 The use-after-free in CommonMakeCurrent() (glx/vndcmds.c) requires
 GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag) to run after CommonMakeNewCurrent() has had a
 chance to realloc cl->contextTags. That ordering was introduced by
 upstream commit 4781f2a5a8c2 ("GLX: Free the tag of the old context
 later", merged 9 Dec 2022). In 1.20.11 (13 Apr 2021) CommonLoseCurrent()
 frees the tag itself on success and CommonMakeCurrent() sets
 oldTag = NULL before CommonMakeNewCurrent() is called, so no dangling
 pointer survives the realloc. The upstream fix only moves the later
 free (added by 4781f2a5) back before CommonMakeNewCurrent(); that code
 does not exist here, so there is nothing to apply. Debian's
 bullseye-security diff through 1.20.11-1+deb11u18 does not touch
 glx/vndcmds.c.
Origin: not-applicable
Bug: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/commit/d6d96084f305a142eb3db7f720d7edd21e4c98b4
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1141703
Author: Root.io <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-10-06

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+# CVE-2026-56000 — Not affected: Debian 11 (bullseye) xorg-server 1.20.11
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| **CVE ID** | CVE-2026-56000 (ZDI-CAN-30561) |
+| **Component** | xorg-server, GLX vendor dispatch (`glx/vndcmds.c`) |
+| **Distribution** | Debian 11 (bullseye) |
+| **Package version** | `xorg-server` `2:1.20.11-1+deb11u17` |
+| **Upstream version** | 1.20.11 (released 13 Apr 2021) |
+| **Upstream fix** | xorg-server 21.1.24 / xwayland 24.1.13 (`2779affbdb43`, `d6d96084f305`) |
+| **Assessment** | **NOT AFFECTED — vulnerable code not present, no code patch required.** |
+
+## What the CVE is
+
+A heap use-after-free in `CommonMakeCurrent()` in `glx/vndcmds.c`.
+`oldTag` is a pointer into the per-client `cl->contextTags` array returned by
+`GlxLookupContextTag()`. In affected versions, `CommonMakeNewCurrent()` is
+called while `oldTag` is still live. `CommonMakeNewCurrent()` calls
+`GlxAllocContextTag()`, which may `realloc()` `cl->contextTags` when all
+slots are in use, moving the array and leaving `oldTag` dangling. The
+subsequent `GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag)` then writes into freed memory.
+
+The upstream fix moves `GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag); oldTag = NULL;` to run
+before `CommonMakeNewCurrent()`.
+
+## Why 1.20.11 is not affected
+
+The vulnerable ordering (free *after* the realloc) was introduced by upstream
+commit `4781f2a5a8c2` ("GLX: Free the tag of the old context later",
+Doğukan Korkmaztürk, 22 Nov 2022, merged 9 Dec 2022). That commit:
+
+- removed `GlxFreeContextTag(tagInfo)` from `CommonLoseCurrent()`
+- removed `oldTag = NULL` after the `CommonLoseCurrent()` call
+- added `GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag); oldTag = NULL;` after `CommonMakeNewCurrent()`
+
+xorg-server 1.20.11 predates that commit by more than a year and still has the
+original ordering. In the 1.20.11 `glx/vndcmds.c`:
+
+```c
+static int CommonLoseCurrent(ClientPtr client, GlxContextTagInfo *tagInfo)
+{
+    int ret;
+
+    ret = tagInfo->vendor->glxvc.makeCurrent(client,
+            tagInfo->tag, // No old context tag,
+            None, None, None, 0);
+
+    if (ret == Success) {
+        GlxFreeContextTag(tagInfo);
+    }
+    return ret;
+}
+```
+
+```c
+        // Clear the old context first.
+        if (oldTag != NULL) {
+            int ret = CommonLoseCurrent(client, oldTag);
+            if (ret != Success) {
+                return ret;
+            }
+            oldTag = NULL;
+        }
+
+        if (newVendor != NULL) {
+            int ret = CommonMakeNewCurrent(client, newVendor, drawable, readdrawable, context, &reply.contextTag);
+            if (ret != Success) {
+                return ret;
+            }
+        } else {
+            reply.contextTag = 0;
+        }
+```
+
+On every path that reaches `CommonMakeNewCurrent()`:
+
+- `CommonLoseCurrent()` returned `Success`, so `GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag)` has
+  already been called on the still-valid pointer, and
+- `oldTag` has been set to `NULL`.
+
+By the time `GlxAllocContextTag()` can `realloc()` `cl->contextTags`, there is
+no stale pointer left to use. If `CommonLoseCurrent()` fails, the function
+returns before `CommonMakeNewCurrent()` is ever called. The use-after-free
+window described by CVE-2026-56000 does not exist in this code.
+
+The upstream fix only moves the later `GlxFreeContextTag(oldTag)` (added by
+`4781f2a5`) back before `CommonMakeNewCurrent()`. That later call is not
+present in 1.20.11, so the fix has nothing to apply to and 1.20.11 is already
+in the fixed ordering.
+
+## Debian packaging
+
+Debian's bullseye security diff through `2:1.20.11-1+deb11u18` does not touch
+`glx/vndcmds.c`, so the Debian package carries the unmodified 1.20.11 code
+shown above.
+
+## Verification
+
+```
+$ git show xorg-server-1.20.11:glx/vndcmds.c | grep -n 'GlxFreeContextTag\|oldTag = NULL\|CommonMakeNewCurrent(client'
+166:        GlxFreeContextTag(tagInfo);          # inside CommonLoseCurrent(), before any realloc
+195:            GlxFreeContextTag(tagInfo);      # CommonMakeNewCurrent() failure path, new tag only
+259:            oldTag = NULL;                   # before CommonMakeNewCurrent()
+263:            int ret = CommonMakeNewCurrent(client, newVendor, drawable, readdrawable, context, &reply.contextTag);
+
+$ git merge-base --is-ancestor 4781f2a5a8c2 xorg-server-1.20.11; echo $?
+1                                                # 4781f2a5 is NOT in 1.20.11
+```
