Description: CVE-2026-50260 - XSYNC use-after-free in FreeCounter()
 A client that sets up multiple SyncCounters and awaits on those triggers can
 trigger a use-after-free when a second client connection destroys those
 counters.
 .
 FreeCounter() iterates the counter's trigger list and invokes the
 CounterDestroyed callback on each trigger. That callback (e.g.
 SyncAwaitTriggerFired -> FreeResource -> FreeAwait) may free the
 SyncAwaitUnion backing those triggers, so reading ptl->next or
 ptl->pTrigger on the next iteration is a use-after-free.
 .
 This change uses the null-terminated list macro so the next pointer stays
 valid, updates pCounter->sync.pTriglist before each callback so FreeAwait sees
 a valid list head, and checks that a trigger is still present before
 dereferencing the callback. It also updates FreeAwait() so that, when the sync
 object is being destroyed, the pTrigger pointer in the trigger list node is
 NULLed out (the backing SyncAwait memory is about to be freed), preventing the
 destroy loop from dereferencing freed memory. This FreeAwait change is the
 shared helper that also backs the miSyncDestroyFence() fix (CVE-2026-50257);
 both originate from the same upstream commit.
 .
 ZDI-CAN-30163 (Trend Micro Zero Day Initiative).
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/commit/f5abfb61994471023d8c6470428c8e30c411cc0b
