Description: CVE-2026-50257 - XSYNC use-after-free in miSyncDestroyFence()
 A client that sets up multiple fence triggers can trigger a use-after-free
 function pointer call: one X connection sets up a fence and awaits it, then a
 second connection destroys the fence, causing the first to dereference freed
 memory.
 .
 miSyncDestroyFence() iterates the fence's trigger list and invokes the
 CounterDestroyed callback on each trigger. That callback (e.g.
 SyncAwaitTriggerFired -> FreeResource -> FreeAwait) may free the
 SyncAwaitUnion backing those triggers, so reading ptl->next or
 ptl->pTrigger on the next iteration is a use-after-free.
 .
 This change uses the null-terminated list macro so the next pointer stays
 valid, updates pFence->sync.pTriglist before each callback so FreeAwait sees a
 valid list head when NULLing out triggers, and checks that a trigger is still
 present before dereferencing the callback.
 .
 The companion FreeAwait() change that NULLs out trigger pointers when the
 sync object is being destroyed is shared with CVE-2026-50260 (FreeCounter)
 and is applied there, since both originate from the same upstream commit.
 .
 ZDI-CAN-30159 (Trend Micro Zero Day Initiative).
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/commit/f5abfb61994471023d8c6470428c8e30c411cc0b
Author: Peter Hutterer <peter.hutterer@who-t.net>
Last-Update: 2026-06-06
---
--- a/miext/sync/misync.c
+++ b/miext/sync/misync.c
@@ -115,10 +115,14 @@ miSyncDestroyFence(SyncFence * pFence)
         SyncScreenPrivPtr pScreenPriv = SYNC_SCREEN_PRIV(pScreen);
         SyncTriggerList *ptl, *pNext;
 
-        /* tell all the fence's triggers that the counter has been destroyed */
-        for (ptl = pFence->sync.pTriglist; ptl; ptl = pNext) {
-            (*ptl->pTrigger->CounterDestroyed) (ptl->pTrigger);
-            pNext = ptl->next;
+        /* tell all the fence's triggers that the fence has been destroyed.
+         * Update pTriglist before each callback and free so that FreeAwait
+         * sees a valid list head when scanning for triggers to NULL out.
+         */
+        nt_list_for_each_entry_safe(ptl, pNext, pFence->sync.pTriglist, next) {
+            pFence->sync.pTriglist = pNext;
+            if (ptl->pTrigger)
+                (*ptl->pTrigger->CounterDestroyed) (ptl->pTrigger);
             free(ptl); /* destroy the trigger list as we go */
         }
 
Description: CVE-2026-34002 - Fix out-of-bounds read in CheckModifierMap()
 The loop in CheckModifierMap() reads from wire without verifying that the
 data is within the request bounds. The req->totalModMapKeys value could
 exceed the actual data provided, causing reads of uninitialized memory.
 This adds a bounds check using _XkbCheckRequestBounds, which requires
 passing a ClientPtr parameter to the (private, static) function.
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/commit/f056ce1cc96ed9261052c31524162c78e458f98c
Author: Olivier Fourdan <ofourdan@redhat.com>
